ed_trans-continental_guide_of_travel%2C_from_the_Atlantic_to_the_Pacific_Ocean_-_containing_full_descriptions_of_railroad_routes_across_the_continent%2C_%2814781046113%29.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=original", "descriptionurl": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:The_Pacific_tourist_-_Adams_and_Bishop%27s_illustrated_trans-continental_guide_of_travel,_from_the_Atlantic_to_the_Pacific_Ocean_-_containing_full_descriptions_of_railroad_routes_across_the_continent,_(14781046113).jpg", "descriptionshorturl": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Special:Redirect/page/44165695", "extmetadata": {"DateTime": {"value": "2015-10-11 18:50:51", "source": "mediawiki-metadata", "hidden": ""}, "ObjectName": {"value": "The Pacific tourist - Adams and Bishop's illustrated trans-continental guide of travel, from the Atlantic to the Pacific Ocean - containing full descriptions of railroad routes across the continent, (14781046113)", "source": "mediawiki-metadata"}, "CommonsMetadataExtension": {"value": 1.2, "source": "extension", "hidden": ""}, "Categories": {"value": "Photos uploaded from Flickr by Fæ using a script|Flickr images reviewed by FlickreviewR|Files from Internet Archive Book Images Flickr stream|Files from Flickr's 'The Commons'|Media needing category review as of 11 October 2015|The Pacific tourist (1881)", "source": "commons-categories", "hidden": ""}, "Assessments": {"value": "", "source": "commons-categories", "hidden": ""}, "ImageDescription": {"value": "<br>\n<p><b>Identifier</b>: pacifictouristad1881shea (<a class=\"external text\" href=\"https://commons.wikimedia.org/w/index.php?title=Special%3ASearch&amp;profile=default&amp;fulltext=Search&amp;search=insource%3A%2Fpacifictouristad1881shea%2F\">find matches</a>)<br>\n<b>Title</b>: <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.flickr.com/photos/internetarchivebookimages/tags/bookidpacifictouristad1881shea\">The Pacific tourist : Adams &amp; Bishop's illustrated trans-continental guide of travel, from the Atlantic to the Pacific Ocean : containing full descriptions of railroad routes across the continent, all pleasure resorts and places of most noted scenery in the Far West, also of all cities, towns, villages, U.S. forts, springs, lakes, mountains, routes of summer travel, best localities for hunting, fishing, sporting, and enjoyment, with all needful information for the pleasure traveler, miner, settler, or business man : a complete traveler's guide of the Union and Central Pacific Railroads, and all points of business or pleasure travel to California, Colorado, Nebraska, Wyoming, Utah, Nevada, Montana, the mines and mining of the Territories, the lands of the Pacific Coast, the wonders of the Rocky Mountains, the scenery of the Sierra Nevadas, the Colorado Mountains, the big trees, the geysers, the Yosemite, and the Yellowstone</a><br>\n<b>Year</b>: <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.flickr.com/photos/internetarchivebookimages/tags/bookyear1881\">1881</a> (<a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.flickr.com/photos/internetarchivebookimages/tags/bookdecade1880\">1880s</a>)<br>\n<b>Authors</b>:  <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.flickr.com/photos/internetarchivebookimages/tags/bookauthorShearer__Frederick_E\">Shearer, Frederick E</a> <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.flickr.com/photos/internetarchivebookimages/tags/bookauthorWilliams__Henry_T\">Williams, Henry T</a><br>\n<b>Subjects</b>:  <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.flickr.com/photos/internetarchivebookimages/tags/booksubjectUnion_Pacific_Railroad_Company\">Union Pacific Railroad Company</a> <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.flickr.com/photos/internetarchivebookimages/tags/booksubjectCentral_Pacific_Railroad_Company\">Central Pacific Railroad Company</a><br>\n<b>Publisher</b>:  <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.flickr.com/photos/internetarchivebookimages/tags/bookpublisherNew_York___Adams___Bishop\">New York : Adams &amp; Bishop</a><br>\n<b>Contributing Library</b>:  <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.flickr.com/photos/internetarchivebookimages/tags/bookcontributorHarold_B__Lee_Library\">Harold B. Lee Library</a><br>\n<b>Digitizing Sponsor</b>:  <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.flickr.com/photos/internetarchivebookimages/tags/booksponsorBrigham_Young_University\">Brigham Young University</a><br>\n<br>\n<b>View Book Page</b>: <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://archive.org/stream/pacifictouristad1881shea/pacifictouristad1881shea#page/n175/mode/1up\">Book Viewer</a><br>\n<b>About This Book</b>: <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://archive.org/details/pacifictouristad1881shea\">Catalog Entry</a><br>\n<b>View All Images</b>: <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.flickr.com/photos/internetarchivebookimages/tags/bookidpacifictouristad1881shea\">All Images From Book</a><br>\nClick here to <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://archive.org/stream/pacifictouristad1881shea/pacifictouristad1881shea#page/n175/mode/1up\"><b>view book online</b></a> to see this illustration in context in a browseable online version of this book.<br>\n<br>\n<b>Text Appearing Before Image:</b><br>\n<i>ide which brings usback nearly to the place we started. A visit toIron Spi-ing Cieek, is well worth taking. Nearits mouth, on the noith side, is the SodaGeysers gi-oup. Fair camjjs are easily found in the LowerGeyser Basin. In the Upper Basin, a good camp for asmall party is in a grove near the Castle. An-other is found about a quarter of a milehigher up. The trail to the Shoshone Geyser Basin leadsup the Fire Hole River, and a short distanceabove the Upper Basin, we pass a fall 60 feethigh, that is worthy a visit from all who vouldsee the beauties as well as the wonders of theregion. It somewhat resembles the Middle Fallat Trenton, New York. Above the falls, thetrail crosses the river to avoid swampy ground,and keeps on the bounding ridge of hills on thewest. The narrow valley expands, and we soonentei- a third geyser basin with several grouj»s ofsprings, and one geyser called the Solitary.It has a dome-sha))ed mound, 15 feet in diam-eter and 11 to 14 feet high, covered with elegant</i><br>\n<b>Text Appearing After Image:</b><br>\n<i>W^B^^UKK^^-j^——z^ iv^! ^m- -^r--^=i::z: -tj-Nirs ^^^^^^</i><br>\n<br>\n<b>Note About Images</b><br>\n</p>\n<i>Please note that these images are extracted from scanned page images that may have been digitally enhanced for readability - coloration and appearance of these illustrations may not perfectly resemble the original work.</i>", "source": "commons-desc-page"}, "DateTimeOriginal": {"value": "1881", "source": "commons-desc-page"}, "Credit": {"value": "<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://www.flickr.com/photos/internetarchivebookimages/14781046113/\">https://www.flickr.com/photos/internetarchivebookimages/14781046113/</a>\n</p>\n<ul><li>Source book page: <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://archive.org/stream/pacifictouristad1881shea/pacifictouristad1881shea#page/n175/mode/1up\">https://archive.org/stream/pacifictouristad1881shea/pacifictouristad1881shea#page/n175/mode/1up</a></li></ul>", "source": "commons-desc-page"}, "Artist": {"value": "<a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.flickr.com/people/126377022@N07\">Internet Archive Book Images</a>", "source": "commons-desc-page"}, "Permission": {"value": "At the time of upload, the image license was automatically confirmed using the Flickr <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/API\" class=\"extiw\" title=\"en:API\">API</a>. For more information see <a href=\"//commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/User:F%C3%A6/Flickr_API_detail\" title=\"